1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Explore Antarctica and Greenland in a shared three-dimensional scientific viewer.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Across Antarctica, bed topography, ice geometry, and fast surface flow appear in one coherent scene.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Hydrology layers add effective pressure and channelized drainage beneath marine-based ice.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
The same visual framework extends to Greenland on a consistent polar grid.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Basin boundaries and velocity patterns reveal how regional flow reorganizes across the ice sheet.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Three-dimensional ocean streamlines connect Greenland's margin to the surrounding Arctic circulation.

7
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Interactive controls switch region, resolution, and layer combinations while the scientific snapshot updates live.

8
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Built for research communication, teaching, and collaboration, the explorer turns polar datasets into an explorable narrative.
